# **Version 1: Recursion with Min/Max (simplest, beginner-friendly)**

```c
/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * struct TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     struct TreeNode *left;
 *     struct TreeNode *right;
 * };
 */

bool check(struct TreeNode* node, long minVal, long maxVal) {
    if (node == NULL) return true;  // Empty node is valid

    if (node->val <= minVal || node->val >= maxVal) 
        return false;

    // Check left and right recursively
    return check(node->left, minVal, node->val) &&
           check(node->right, node->val, maxVal);
}

bool isValidBST(struct TreeNode* root) {
    return check(root, -10000000000, 10000000000);  // Large range for beginners
}
```

**Logic:**  
- Each node must be in the `(minVal, maxVal)` range.  
- Recurse left/right with updated min/max.  

---

# **Version 2: Recursion with LONG_MIN / LONG_MAX (standard C)**

```c
#include <limits.h>
#include <stdbool.h>

/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * struct TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     struct TreeNode *left;
 *     struct TreeNode *right;
 * };
 */

bool helper(struct TreeNode* node, long minVal, long maxVal) {
    if (node == NULL) return true;
    if (node->val <= minVal || node->val >= maxVal) return false;
    return helper(node->left, minVal, node->val) &&
           helper(node->right, node->val, maxVal);
}

bool isValidBST(struct TreeNode* root) {
    return helper(root, LONG_MIN, LONG_MAX);
}
```

**Logic:** Same as Version 1, just uses **LONG_MIN / LONG_MAX** instead of arbitrary large numbers.

---

# **Version 3: Inorder Traversal (Non-recursive alternative for beginners)**

**Idea:** BST inorder traversal gives **sorted values**.  
- Traverse tree inorder.  
- Keep track of **previous node value**.  
- If current value ≤ previous value → not BST.

```c
#include <stdbool.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * struct TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     struct TreeNode *left;
 *     struct TreeNode *right;
 * };
 */

bool inorder(struct TreeNode* root, long* prev) {
    if (!root) return true;

    if (!inorder(root->left, prev)) return false;

    if (root->val <= *prev) return false; // BST property violated
    *prev = root->val;

    return inorder(root->right, prev);
}

bool isValidBST(struct TreeNode* root) {
    long prev = -10000000000; // start smaller than any node value
    return inorder(root, &prev);
}
```

**Logic:**  
- Left → Node → Right (inorder)  
- Node values must strictly increase  

